+CONDITIONAL TEMPLATE PROPOSITION CHECK
+Use this branch only for the already permitted template conditions: equivalent
+generic marketing copy without concrete item specifications; the same short
+generic cookie/services/advertising/visits message with unchanged behavior; or
+complete retained cookie definitions with stock framing or covered repetition.
+Check the remaining actual assertions, not merely the changed category/name.
+Keep the real names truthful. A permitted category/provider slot alone does not
+establish another actual product record, purpose, restriction or liable party.
+An unnamed provider can express the same generic behavior as a named slot in
+the permitted short notice; do not invent a new behavior from naming alone.
+
+Within this qualified stock-template branch, search the whole other document
+for each complete proposition. A stock paragraph already covered elsewhere is
+still covered when repeated beneath a standard category heading. The heading
+alone does not create another processing rule from that same stock paragraph.
+A bare terms/menu label or reference supplies no unshown legal conditions.
+Concrete additional deployment details, data flows, transfer/storage limits,
+retention periods, consent mechanisms and actual obligations remain useful.
+An independent extra explanation is not a conflicting value in the shared text.
+
+Do not decide by which text seems more accurate, better written or preferable
+to keep. Compare the asserted contributions under this policy; do not correct
+the source or discard an assertion merely because it seems mistaken. A positive
+coverage conclusion needs an actual retained equivalent proposition or an
+applicable harmless exception, not a preference for the other document.
+
+This branch does not exempt actual named items or populated records, literal
+submission/payment/account routes, changed procedures/capabilities/conditions,
+named liability parties or substantive body versions in different languages.
+The existing mechanism-qualified form-localization branch remains separate.
+
+DERIVE THE NATIVE COVERAGE FIELDS FOR THIS QUALIFIED BRANCH
+Choose a loss ID only for an actual uncovered useful contribution after that
+whole-document check. If a side has only permitted slots/framing/repetition,
+its loss ID is empty, even when it has unique lexical span IDs. If the other
+side adds a concrete deployment explanation, select loss only on the side with
+that uncovered addition. The already covered stock paragraph is not another
+loss or conflict. Use conflict=NONE when the difference is only an independent
+addition. Keep a real nonempty context ID for each side and truthful retained
+overlap basis. Your explanation and loss selections must describe the same
+actual coverage; a string difference or bare terms heading cannot justify loss.
+
